\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Finite trace-selection experiment}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{harness}

\p{The selective-refinement study compares fixed-horizon data interventions
under a declared training and evaluation boundary
\citet{Sections 6-7; Tables 4-5, 10}{dang2026selecting}. A
\newvocab{trace-selection experiment} is the following finite typed record.}

\p{Fix the P0 lifecycle arm set #{\mathcal A}, its boundary map
#{r:\mathcal A\to\mathcal J}, mask map
#{M:\mathcal A\to\mathcal P(\{s,h,w\})}, and endowment #{E_0} from
\ref{ftip-00P0} and \ref{ftip-00OY}. Choose finite nonempty label sets}
##{
\mathfrak H\subset\mathbb N,\qquad
\mathfrak L,\qquad
\mathfrak B\subset\mathbb N_{>0},\qquad
\mathfrak D,\qquad
\mathfrak R.
}
\p{A split map returns a triple}
##{
\operatorname{split}:\mathfrak D\longrightarrow
\{(Q_{\rm sel},Q_{\rm hold},Q_{\rm xb})\mid
Q_{\rm sel},Q_{\rm hold},Q_{\rm xb}\subseteq\mathcal Q\text{ are finite}\},
}
\p{whose three outputs are pairwise disjoint and satisfy
#{|Q_{\rm sel}|>0}, #{|Q_{\rm hold}|>0}; #{Q_{\rm xb}} may be empty only
when the experiment records that no cross-benchmark comparison is made. A
randomization map
#{\lambda_{\rm pair}:\mathfrak R\to\operatorname{Dist}(\mathcal G\times\mathcal G)}
supplies a joint source law for each paired comparison.}

\p{The experiment declares a finite, nonempty arm set
#{\mathfrak A\subseteq\mathcal A\times\mathfrak H\times\mathfrak L\times
\mathfrak B\times\mathfrak D\times\mathfrak R}. For each
#{a\in\mathfrak A}, write its projections as}
##{
(a_0(a),H_a,\ell_a,B_a,D_a,\eta_a),\qquad
r_a:=r(a_0(a)),\quad M_a:=M(a_0(a)),\quad
\mathcal R_a:=\lambda_{\rm pair}(\eta_a).
}
\p{The arm record additionally supplies one model, teacher, scaffold,
verifier, task law, inference protocol, and componentwise budget. These
objects are maps of #{a}, not implicit labels; paired arms must agree on every
object except the factor named by their comparison. The split attached to
#{D_a} is written #{(Q_{\rm sel,a},Q_{\rm hold,a},Q_{\rm xb,a})}; it also
supplies a nonempty finite strategy-label set #{\mathfrak S_a} and a receipt
space #{\mathcal R_a^{\rm rec}} containing a typed held-out outcome
#{Y_a\in\mathcal Y_a\cup\{\bot\}} and an admission field. For every paired
comparison #{(a,a')}, the record additionally declares the finite pairing
space
#{\mathcal P_{a,a'}:=(Q_{\rm hold,a}\cap Q_{\rm hold,a'})
\times\mathfrak S_a\times\mathfrak S_{a'}}
and a law #{\Lambda_{a,a'}} on
#{\mathcal G\times\mathcal G\times\mathcal P_{a,a'}}. The shared task
coordinate in this law is the pairing key; the two strategy coordinates may
differ.}

\p{For each arm, let #{\mathcal X^{\rm sel}_a} be the finite candidate-pool
space with #{1\leq B_a\leq|\mathcal X^{\rm sel}_a|}, and let
#{\mathcal F^{\rm sel}_a} be the sigma-field generated by the
selection-time prefix, teacher-forced score, data-only trace metadata, and
#{Q_{\rm sel,a}}. The metadata map excludes held-out outcomes, verifier
outcomes, and post-selection continuation events. The selector is a measurable
kernel with respect to this sigma-field}
##{
\mathsf S_{a,\ell_a}:\mathcal X^{\rm sel}_a
\longrightarrow\operatorname{Dist}\bigl(\{I\subseteq\mathcal X^{\rm sel}_a:
|I|=B_a\}\bigr).
}
\p{It therefore returns a retained index set of the declared size without
access to held-out outcomes. Write
#{\mathcal I_a:=\{I\subseteq\mathcal X^{\rm sel}_a:|I|=B_a\}}. A run kernel}
##{
\mathsf K^{\rm run}_{a,\ell_a}:
\mathcal X^{\rm sel}_a\times\mathcal I_a\times\mathcal G
\times\mathcal Q\times\mathfrak S_a
\longrightarrow\operatorname{Dist}(\mathcal R_a^{\rm rec})
}
\p{maps a candidate pool, its retained index set, one component of the
paired source draw, a task, and its arm-specific strategy coordinate to a
receipt with an event sequence, task and strategy labels, final verifier
outcome, typed held-out outcome, admission field, state and artifact hashes,
and the charged token, tool, storage, restart, discarded trace, and
verification costs, with exactly #{H_a+1} event slots and a timeout receipt
at the final slot when needed. For a paired comparison, #{\Lambda_{a,a'}}
supplies a common held-out task and the two strategy coordinates, while
#{\mathcal R_a} supplies the two source components before the kernels are
applied. Thus an arm defines maps and kernels that use the selector output to
produce replayable receipts; it does not merely list factors whose later
meaning is left implicit.}

\p{The reset transition is #{\mathsf{Reset}_{r_a,M_a}} from
\ref{ftip-00P0}. Horizon, selector, budget, split, and randomization are
therefore attached to a concrete P0 state boundary and a concrete run kernel.
This is an empirical protocol definition, not a theorem or a claim that any
selector improves behavior.}
